\par\par \b \uc2 European Morning Briefing: Stocks Seen Higher; Focus on Ukraine, China\b0\par\par\uc2 4,978 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SNAPSHOT:\par \par \uc2 ========\par \par \uc2 European bourses seen higher, bunds and gilts mixed; euro, oil mixed, spot gold up slightly\par \par \uc2 -Shell Gas To Focus On Larger Projects As It Cuts Spending\par \par \uc2 -\uc2 Barclays\uc2 , \uc2 China Development Bank\uc2  Ink New Pact\par \par \uc2 -Deutsche Banker Who Committed Suicide Anxious Amid Probes\par \par \uc2 -\uc2 Facebook\uc2  to Acquire Virtual Reality Company for $2 Billion\par \par \uc2 -Left Alliance Quits Finland Government Over Austerity Measures\par \par \uc2 -WATCH FOR: German, Italian consumer confidence; ECB's Draghi, France's Hollande meet; U.S. durable goods, services PMI, weekly oil data\par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN OUTLOOK & U.S./ASIAN SUMMARIES:\par \par \uc2 ========\par \par \uc2 Investors hoping for stimulus from China and the eurozone, are looking for slightly higher stock markets in Europe, with bunds and gilts mixed, while watching for developments around Ukraine to unfold.\par \par \uc2 President Barack Obama will meet European allies and NATO officials in Brussels on Wednesday, following a session in The Hague at which members of the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  leading nations adopted a formal statement condemning \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and annexation of the Crimea region of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The future of natural gas supply in central Europe will be discussed at a conference Wednesday, while the U.S. and the Czech Republic will cement their ties in nuclear energy.\par \par \uc2 Officials from Europe's gas sector, wary of potential disruptions to deliveries of Russian gas after Russia's recent annexation of Crimea, will meet in Prague to discuss how the sector should best position itself given the uncertain outlook.\par \par \uc2 Stocks rallied across Asia on Wednesday, tracking gains in U.S. shares after consumer confidence in the world's largest economy rose to an over six-year high. However, traders say the gains could be fleeting as the focus turns to local factors.\par \par \uc2 Wall Street futures were slightly higher, with Treasurys hardly changed, as the euro and oil futures traded little changed, while spot gold edged higher.\par \par \uc2 STOCKS:\par \par \uc2 ======\par \par \uc2 Stock markets may start higher on hopes for stimulus measures from China and the eurozone after \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials offered dovish views.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the opening, IG has called the FTSE up 17 at 6621, the DAX up 43 at 9381, and the CAC up 21 at 4365.\par \par \uc2 "The comments sound somewhat more open-minded to the idea of additional policy action from the ECB," said Ken Wattret, co-head of European market economics at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As for China, "the market has shifted focus away from growth concerns and toward possible policy steps by Chinese authorities to stem the economic weakness," said analysts at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The bets are growing that further stimulus measures across Europe and China will be introduced over the coming months," noted IG strategist Evan Lucas.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stock futures were higher Wednesday, after benchmarks rose Tuesday, breaking a two-session slide in choppy trading that saw the market's recent highflying names swerve between gains and losses.\par \par \uc2 Some market watchers said the abrupt weakness in highflying stocks appeared to be the work of long-term investors booking profits before the end of the first quarter. Others said the selloff in strong-performing stocks represents an ominous signal that investors are girding for additional market declines.\par \par \uc2 "When you start to see momentum leadership reverse, it is usually the first stage of some type of risk-off mode," said Mike O'Rourke, chief market strategist at \uc2 JonesTrading Institutional Services\uc2 . Recent selling in biotech has "filtered through all the momentum stocks as well," Mr. O'Rourke said, including internet stocks. "There is no compelling reason to be aggressive right now."\par \par \uc2 On the data front, traders will look for U.S. durable goods data figures due at 1230 GMT. "We expect durable goods orders to increase m-o-m by 1.0 percent in February, versus a decline of 1.0 percent in January," Handelsbanken said. "The ISM manufacturing's new order component, which is a leading indicator of durable goods orders, was on strong 54.5 in February," it noted.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 ======\par \par \uc2 The euro was mixed against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia after a slew of policy makers from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  decried the strength of the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and offered measures to stem the risk of deflation.\par \par \uc2 "People keep trying to buy dollars, but they get frustrated because it keeps snapping back on them," said Brad Bechtel, managing director at Faros Trading. He added that trading flows may ramp up as month-end and quarter-end buying takes place.\par \par \uc2 BONDS:\par \par \uc2 =====\par \par \uc2 Bunds may start mixed as investors get the latest readings of consumer confidence in embattled Italy and flourishing Germany amid speculation about monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Setting a negative deposit rate to guard against excessively low inflation is an option for the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said \uc2 Finland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Erkki Liikanen, the latest indication that officials are willing to provide fresh stimulus to protect a fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasurys were little changed Wednesday, after government bonds on Tuesday edged higher as a round of mixed U.S. economic releases deflated concerns that the Federal Reserve could raise interest rates sooner than expected.\par \par \uc2 A $32 billion sale of two-year notes also saw strong demand.\par \par \uc2 The selling in short-dated bonds is "overdone in the short term," said Charles Comiskey, head of Treasury trading at \uc2 Bank of Nova Scotia\uc2  in New York. "The timing for the first rate hike from the Fed depends on upcoming economic data."\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia President Charles Plosser said the time to think about raising short-term interest rates may well have arrived.\par \par \uc2 In Japan Wednesday, government bonds edged higher as the fiscal year approaches its close.\par \par \uc2 ENERGY:\par \par \uc2 =======\par \par \uc2 Oil prices were little changed amid a range of U.S. and international factors, including continued geopolitical tensions over the Ukraine and cleanup efforts from an oil spill in a major U.S. shipping channel.\par \par \uc2 "Oil is just fluctuating in response to myriad items here," analyst Jim Ritterbusch said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are expecting another increase in domestic oil inventories in data to be released Wednesday by the \uc2 U.S. Energy Information Administration\uc2 , with a consensus estimate of 2.8 million barrels, according to a survey of analysts by The Wall Street Journal. Crude stockpiles have risen as refineries have reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  during spring maintenance season.\par \par \uc2 Nymex crude was unchanged at $99.28, while Brent was off 2 cents at $106.97.\par \par \uc2 METALS:\par \par \uc2 ======\par \par \uc2 Base metals could be rangebound as they look for cues, but expectations of stimulus measures from the Chinese government could help to provide a floor for prices. The market is "most likely already pricing in this slower growth," in China, the world's biggest consumer of industrial metals, Walter de Wet, analyst at Standard Bank, said in a report. He expected China's economic growth to slow over the next three years and said the current slump in growth momentum was cyclical.\par \par \uc2 LME 3-month copper was up $5.75 at $6,577/ton.\par \par \uc2 Gold edged higher in Asia with modest physical demand helping to underpin prices. "Better physical demand suggests there may be a turn in momentum in the coming days," ANZ said in a report. Spot gold prices have slipped about 5.6% from its six-month high this month as geopolitical tensions in Ukraine eased and U.S. Federal Reserve's stance suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may start raising the interest rate sooner than the market expects. Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia President Charles Plosser said the time to think about raising short-term interest rates may well have arrived.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold was at $1,313.90/oz, up $2.80.\par \par \uc2 Write to Dennis Baker at dennis.baker@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 26 Mar 2014 01:00 EDT  European Morning Briefing: DJ Dominant Headlines; Other Top Stories\par \par \uc2 DJ Dominant Headlines:\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , \uc2 China Development Bank\uc2  Ink New Pact\par \par \uc2 SEC Set to Alter Stance on Money Funds\par \par \uc2 Apple Engineer Recalls the iPhone's Birth\par \par \uc2 Investigators Trying To Understand Significance Of Last Partial Transmission --Inmarsat Executive\par \par \uc2 StubHub Sings the Blues After Shifting Fees\par \par \uc2 Other Top Stories:\par \par \uc2 Australia \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sees Stable Rates\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. Glenn Stevens said a period of record low interest rates would likely continue for a while, but warned the economic outlook Down Under was uncertain as a mining-investment boom fades.\par \par \uc2 Australia Ramps Up Warnings on Surging House Prices\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue to monitor a surge in speculative lending for property, saying some measures of real-estate risk appetite resemble boom-like conditions.\par \par \uc2 Search Resumes for Flight 370 Wreckage\par \par \uc2 The race to find \uc2 Malaysia Airlines\uc2  Flight 370, now assumed lost in the southern Indian Ocean, resumed Wednesday as a break in the weather allowed authorities to direct a dozen aircraft into the search zone.\par \par \uc2 Left Alliance Quits Finland Government Over Austerity Measures\par \par \uc2 Finland's decision to launch a fresh round of austerity measures to halt growth in public debt resulted in a junior partner quitting the country's six-party coalition government late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Everbright Securities\uc2  2013 Net Profit Falls 79% on Investment Losses\par \par \uc2 Everbright Securities Co\uc2 . (601788.SH) said Wednesday that 2013 net profit fell 79% from a year earlier due to investment losses from a trading glitch and regulatory fines.\par \par \uc2 Leaders of South Korea, Japan Meet for First Time\par \par \uc2 The leaders of South Korea and Japan met for the first time since each came to power more than a year ago, joining President Barack Obama for a meeting that avoided historical issues and focused on North Korea.\par \par \uc2 Hyundai Motor\uc2  to Build a New Plant In China\par \par \uc2 Hyundai Motor\uc2  said it plans to build a new production plant in Chongqing, China, to expand its share of the world's largest automobile market.\par \par \uc2 26 Mar 2014 01:00 EDT  European Morning Briefing: Market Prices, Data Calendar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DJIA    16367.88  +91.19 +0.56% \par Nasdaq   4234.27   +7.88 +0.19%