\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE- \highlight22\uc2 Central bank \highlight\uc2  says Russia will not impose capital controls\b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says policies provide financial stability\par \par \uc2 * Finance ministry would oppose capital controls\par \par \uc2 * Capital fight expected at $50-$70 billion in first quarter\par \par \uc2 By Oksana Kobzeva and Lidia Kelly\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 18 (Reuters) - Russia will not impose capital controls, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday, easing concerns that restrictions could be introduced to stem capital flight that has accelerated since the Ukrainian region of Crimea was seized by Russian forces.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's assertions of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rights to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine and make Crimea part of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to cause net capital outflows in the first quarter to $50-$70 billion, compared with $63 billion in the whole of last year.\par \par \uc2 Limiting money flows, once considered a damaging constraint on open markets, has been more accepted in the aftermath of the 2008-2009 financial crisis as a tool sometimes needed to manage financial stability.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its current monetary policy is strong enough to provide financial stability and the issue of capital controls is not on the table.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Russia is not considering at this time the possibility of introducing measures that would restrict the movement of the capital," the bank told Reuters in an emailed statement.\par \par \uc2 "Actions taken by the Bank of Russia in the framework of exchange rate policy help contain excessive exchange rate fluctuations, and as such prevent the emergence of risks to financial stability."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been gradually allowing the rouble to float more freely, had to halt the process earlier this month and start defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has lost more than a tenth of its value this year.\par \par \uc2 Introducing restrictions on money flows would reduce Russians' demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it would also raise borrowing costs for the state and corporations alike.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry has spent the past few years building up the country's debt by successfully raising billions in foreign borrowing. This year's plans envisage another $7 billion worth of Eurobonds.\par \par \uc2 "If such an idea (capital controls) were to be discussed, the finance ministry would be against it," Deputy Finance Minister Alexei Moiseev, responsible for financial markets, told Reuters on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 POLITICAL DECISION\par \par \uc2 The Russian rouble has been weakening since the start of the year, along with the Turkish lira and other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's declaration in early March of its right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine has accelerated the rouble's fall, costing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than $20 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend it.\par \par \uc2 "When any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling its reserves, one wonders how long it is going to continue its policy. One of the alternatives to not spending reserves is capital controls," said Alexander Morozov, chief Russia economist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Russia's gold and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's fifth-largest, stand at $494 billion, giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  some room to manoeuvre.\par \par \uc2 But Morozov, who also said there is no need for now for any capital restrictions, reckons there is also a political reason behind the stance of monetary officials.\par \par \uc2 Russia introduced capital account liberalisation only in 2006, spending years to repair the damage caused by the financial chaos after the fall of the Soviet Union in the 1990s.\par \par \uc2 "It was done to make the Russian economy open as an OECD (\uc2 Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development\uc2 ) economy and it's still one of the more paramount political objectives of the Russian political leadership," Morozov said.\par \par \uc2 "Any stepping back would be like an admission of failure, so it's a political issue."\par \par \uc2 MONETARY POLICY\par \par \uc2 Morozov and other economists in Russia also believe that there is no economic reason to introduce capital controls.\par \par \uc2 In the aftermath of the 2008 financial crisis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  went through $200 billion of its reserves, but without having to introduce capital controls.\par \par \uc2 On March 3, after Russia's parliament backed possible military action in Ukraine, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced abruptly to raise its key lending rate by 150 basis points to stem capital flight. It also said it would make daily decisions on regulating the rouble's exchange rate, increasing its scope to make \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes these moves are sufficient for now.\par \par \uc2 The policy, based on "an assessment of the current situation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, allows (the bank) to respond quickly to sudden changes in the situation," the bank said in its statement.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep employing more conventional monetary policy for the time being.\par \par \uc2 "Unless capital outflows stabilise, further rate hikes are possible," said Neil Shearing, chief emerging market economist at Capital Economics in London. (Additional reporting by Darya Korsunskaya; Writing by Lidia Kelly; Editing by Jason Bush and Giles Elgood)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-21T10:50:18.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140318ea3i00bt1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
