\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS BROADLY HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks rose as investors took Crimea's widely expected vote to secede from Ukraine in stride. European markets also gained ground, with Russian stocks rallying to snap a four-session losing streak. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOSCOW SIGNALS IT WILL ANNEX CRIMEA QUICKLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia gave its clearest signal yet that it plans to move fast to annex Crimea, defying U.S. and European threats of sanctions a day after a referendum in the breakaway Ukrainian region to secede passed handily. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VODAFONE TO ACQUIRE SPAIN'S ONO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vodafone\f28 \uc2 \f2  has agreed to acquire Spanish cable company Ono for \u8364\'20\'AC7.2 billion, in an attempt to expand further into Western Europe, one of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vodafone\f28 \uc2 \f2 's main markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NUMBER OF COUNTRIES SEARCHING FOR FLIGHT 370 DOUBLES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The search for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia Airlines\f28 \uc2 \f2  Flight 370 expanded by thousands of miles in an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of unprecedented scale, marked by a series of twists that have made the least likely scenarios the most credible. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION REBOUNDS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial production increased a seasonally adjusted 0.6% in February from January, while capacity utilization rose 0.3 percentage point to a 78.8% rate. Economists forecast output would rise 0.1% and a utilization rate of 78.5%. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YUAN WEAKENS AS PBOC DOUBLES TRADING BAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese yuan fell to lowest level in 10 months after the country allowed its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to trade more freely, hitting levels that sparked rapidly accumulating losses for investors who made leveraged bets the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would keep appreciating. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU TO PROBE LIBERTY GLOBAL BUY OF ZIGGO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The EU's antitrust authority will review \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liberty Global\f28 \uc2 \f2 's planned \u8364\'20\'AC6.9 billion acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ziggo\f28 \uc2 \f2 , kicking off a formal process as investors look for clues to the regulator's approach to Europe's rapidly-consolidating telecoms industry. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW YORK FED MARCH MANUFACTURING INDEX EDGES UP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York manufacturers say business conditions improved this month, although new demand remains sluggish, according to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Empire State Manufacturing Survey. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. FORCES TAKE CONTROL OF LIBYAN TANKER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. forces boarded an oil tanker loaded with Libyan crude and took control of the vessel, ending an affair started a week ago when the ship left a rebel-controlled Libyan port. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE INFLATION LOWER THAN FIRST ESTIMATED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's annual rate of inflation was lower in February than first estimated, and fell back to the level reached in October 2013 that prompted the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's last effort to stimulate growth. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL FUTURES SAG AS CONCERNS ABOUT SANCTIONS EASE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices slipped as market watchers anticipated that potential western sanctions against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to the nation's military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Ukraine wouldn't affect global energy supplies. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par  \par The Wall Street Journal \par BUSINESS FINDS NEW REASON FOR OPTIMISM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Worries over the upheaval in Crimea are rising, along with fears of an economic slowdown in China. But another drag on optimism--business uncertainty--is heading the other way. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Al's Emporium \par ILL-SUITED FOR SUITS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mark 2014 as the year that sales of the business suit peaked, Al Lewis writes. The defining moment: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Men's Wearhouse\f28 \uc2 \f2 's $1.8 billion deal to buy Jos. A. Bank Clothiers, purveyor of the "Buy One, Get Seven Free" sale \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 17, 2014 10:00 ET (14:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140317ea3h001r2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
