\par\par \b \uc2 Asian Morning Briefing: U.S. Stocks Fall Again, Treasurys Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 1,847 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 22:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MARKETS AT A GLANCE: \par (Data as of approximately 5 p.m. ET Friday) \par  \par                     LAST        CHANGE  %CHG \par DJIA                16065.67    -43.22  -0.27% \par Nasdaq              4245.40     -15.02  -0.35% \par S&P 500             1841.13     -5.21   -0.28% \par Japan: Nikkei 225   14327.66    -488.32 -3.30% \par Hang Seng           21539.49    -216.59 -1.00% \par Shanghai Composite  2004.34     -14.77  -0.73% \par S&P BSE Sensex      21809.80    35.19   0.16% \par Australia: S&P/ASX  5329.40     -83.20  -1.54% \par UK: FTSE 100        6527.89     -25.89  -0.40% \par  \par                     PRICE CHG   YIELD \par U.S. 2 Year         -0/32       0.346 \par U.S. 5 Year         -2/32       1.538 \par U.S. 10 Year        -3/32       2.657 \par Australia 10 Year   1 1/32      4.048 \par China 10 Year       3/32        4.460 \par India 10 Year       -5/32       8.795 \par Japan 10 Year       6/32        0.624 \par German 10 Year      -2/32       1.549 \par  \par                         LAST(MID)   CHANGE \par Australia $ (AUD/USD)   0.9032      0.0003 \par Yen (USD/JPY)           101.36      -0.48 \par S. Korean Won (USD/KRW) 1070.95     1.05 \par Chinese Yuan (USD/CNY)  6.1496      0.0141 \par Euro (EUR/USD)          1.3912      0.0041 \par WSJ Dollar Index        73.08       -0.19 \par  \par                 LAST    CHANGE  %CHG \par Crude Oil       99.03   0.83    0.85% \par Brent Crude     108.24  1.32    1.23% \par Gold            1383.0  10.6    0.77% \par  \par SNAPSHOT: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rising tensions in Ukraine sent U.S. stocks lower and oil, gold and Treasurys higher Friday. The yen strengthened against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid demand for assets seen as less risky after talks broke down between U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry and Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OPENING CALL: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fallout from Alibaba's decision to list on a U.S. Stock exchange will continue. Already, the head of the jilted Hong Kong stock exchange is urging regulators to change rules to accommodate new listings. The loss of e-commerce giant Alibaba, and potentially one of the biggest initial public offerings in history, comes as the Hong Kong Exchange has missed out on a wave of Chinese tech IPOs. Nine of the 10 biggest IPOs by Chinese Internet-related companies since 2009 have been in the U.S., according to data provider Dealogic. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EQUITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks slumped Friday, capping their biggest weekly loss since late January, as disappointing domestic economic data and continued political turmoil in Ukraine kept buyers sidelined.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Geopolitical tensions kept investors on edge ahead of a Sunday vote in Crimea, which will determine whether the majority ethnic-Russian region secedes from Ukraine and joins Russia. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the U.S. have called the referendum illegal and are expected to impose sanctions on Russia Monday unless it backs down from its stance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although the crisis doesn't have a direct bearing on U.S. stocks, investors say they are worried about the prospect of an escalation that results in economic sanctions or that threatens Europe's economic recovery. One fear that investors have raised is the possibility that Russia will curb its energy supplies to the continent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Headlines around some of the geopolitical emerging-market issues have traders playing the momentum day-to-day," said Doug Crofton, managing director in cash equity trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In corporate news, \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Mills\f28 \uc2 \f2  slid 2.4% after the Cheerios cereal and Green Giant frozen vegetables seller gave a disappointing quarterly earnings forecast, citing lower sales volumes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Nikkei Stock Average slid 3.3% Friday, the biggest one-day loss since Feb. 4, while China's Shanghai Composite fell 0.7%.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen strengthened against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as growing uncertainty stemming from China's economic slowdown and rising tensions in Ukraine buoyed demand for assets seen as less risky.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The geopolitical backdrop generated some stresses in some financial markets, and the yen benefited from this," said Robert Lynch, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors remained on edge after talks between U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry and Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov broke down on Friday ahead of this weekend's vote on Crimea's secession from Ukraine. Russian soldiers had massed along the border with Ukraine, ramping up tension between the two nations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, disappointing economic numbers from China have unnerved investors fearing a slowdown in the world's second-largest economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BONDS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury bonds rose for a fifth straight session Friday, marking the longest winning streak for the 10-year note since September, as worries over Ukraine's political crisis and China's slowing economy buoyed haven assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The bond market continues to benefit from nervousness that something could explode in Crimea or Eastern Ukraine over the weekend as well as ongoing concern about China's growth and credit bubble," said Anthony Cronin, a Treasury bond trader at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The 10-year yield, a benchmark for setting borrowing costs for consumers and businesses, fell by 0.14 percentage points this week, posting its biggest weekly decline since September. The yield had reached a six-week peak of 2.821% last Friday following a better-than-expected U.S. jobs report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury yields could fall further if Ukraine's crisis spins out of control and the bond market's price strength hinges on the degree to which geopolitical tensions would affect the global economic outlook. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COMMODITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil futures rose but ended lower for the week as traders who had bet on lower prices closed out their positions due to concern that tensions between Russia and Ukraine could worsen over the weekend.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Talks between U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry and Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov over Crimea broke down Friday. A referendum on Crimea seceding from Ukraine and joining Russia is scheduled for Sunday. Western leaders have threatened to impose sanctions if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not reduce its military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Crimea.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market's taking somewhat of a wary eye towards Ukraine," said Andy Lebow, senior vice president for energy at Jefferies Bache.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices closed at the highest level in six months as investors remained cautious over the fluid geopolitical situation in Ukraine. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S HEADLINES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Readies U.S. IPO\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group Holding Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said on Sunday it plans to start the process of listing on a U.S. stock exchange, as it prepares to launch one of the largest public offerings in U.S. history.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Early Results: Crimeans Vote to Join Russia\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crimeans voted overwhelmingly on Sunday to break away from Ukraine and join Russia, according to preliminary results, in a referendum that the West condemned as illegal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Senate Lawmakers Unveil Bill to Eliminate Fannie, Freddie\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Senate lawmakers released their first draft of a bipartisan bill Sunday spelling out their proposal, previously announced last week, to eliminate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fannie Mae\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Freddie Mac\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The legislation replaces the mortgage-finance giants with a new system in which the government would continue to play a potentially significant role insuring U.S. home loans.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia to Investigate Flight 370's Transponders\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian authorities are looking into why the transponders on Flight 370 stopped transmitting data, including the possibility they were deliberately switched off, amid new information that showed the plane continued flying for hours after it fell off civilian radar a week ago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Weibo Files Papers for U.S. IPO\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 -like service \f28 \uc2 \f2 Weibo Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has filed plans to raise up to $500 million in an initial public offering in the U.S., with plans to use proceeds to repay loans and invest in technology and marketing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nokia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Loses India Tax Appeal\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's top court dismissed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's recent appeal of a lower court order related to a continuing tax dispute that has cast a shadow over the Finnish company's $7.5 billion deal to sell its handset business to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed's Balance Sheet Hit $4 Trillion at End of 2013\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve's balance sheet grew to $4 trillion at the end of last year, and the larger securities holdings earned it enough interest to remit $79.6 billion to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FDIC Sues Major Banks Over Role in Libor Manipulation\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Deposit Insurance Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is suing major U.S. and international banks such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 , J.P. Morgan Chase and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  for their alleged role in manipulating world-wide interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Producer Prices Fall, Signaling Weak Inflation\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The producer-price index, which measures price changes for everything from food to energy to transportation services, decreased 0.1% from the prior month. That compared to the 0.2% rise forecast by economists.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Consumer Sentiment Takes Surprise Turn Down\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thomson-Reuters/\f28 \uc2 \f2 University of Michigan\f28 \uc2 \f2  preliminary March sentiment index unexpectedly slipped to 79.9 from an end-February reading of 81.6, showing U.S. consumers began feeling more worried about their economic future..\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Berkshire Investors to Vote on Dividend Proposal\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Berkshire Hathaway\f28 \uc2 \f2  will vote on a shareholder proposal calling on the company's directors to consider paying a "meaningful" annual dividend, according to Berkshire's annual proxy filing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vivendi in Exclusive Talks With Altice on SFR\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vivendi said that it has entered exclusive talks with cable holding company Altice to sell the bulk of its cellphone arm SFR in a deal that would leave its French rivals continuing to struggle in a tough price war. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RECENT DJ DOMINANTS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Encana in Advanced Talks to Sell Wyoming Asset to Carlyle, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Natural Gas Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  -- Sources\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business Finds New Reason for Optimism\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PBOC Sharply Widens Yuan Trading Band\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tunisia Focusing on Economic Growth: Prime Minister\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GoDaddy Prepares for Initial Public Offering, Sources Say\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daimler, Nissan Eying Joint Car Assembly Venture in Mexico\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Advent International\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sees Brazilian Investment Opportunities for Private Equity\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Austria Rules Out Hypo Insolvency\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 16 Mar 2014 17:35 EDT \par Asian Morning Briefing: U.S. Stocks Fall Again, -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Easing Sanctions Boost Iran's Petrochemical Sales To Asia--Iran Exec \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Times in GMT, followed by country and event)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2100 SKA Feb Department store sales\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2100 NZ Q1 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  McDermott Miller Consumer Confidence Index\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2130 NZ Feb BNZ - BusinessNZ Performance of Services Index (PS)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0030 SIN Feb Merchandise Trade, incl non-oil domestic exports (NODX)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0030 AUS Feb New Motor Vehicle Sales\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0200 CHN Feb FDI Foreign Direct Investment\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0300 SKA Q4 Non-financial company outstanding debt\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0800 HK Feb Hong Kong port container throughput monthly estimates\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0830 HK Feb Unemployment\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0830 HK Feb Underemployment\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1000 EU Feb Harmonized CPI\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1100 FRA Q4 OECD Quarterly National Accounts G20 GDP growth\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1100 GER Mar Bundesbank monthly report\f28 \