\par\par \b \uc2 METALS-London copper near 3 month low; more losses eyed on Russia\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 02:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, March 4 (Reuters) - London copper steadied on Tuesday, holding not far off three-month lows touched the day before as widespread risk aversion tainted sentiment already damaged by signs of shrinking manufacturing growth in top metals user China.                              \par \par \uc2 FUNDAMENTALS               \par \par \uc2 * Three-month copper on the London Metal Exchange  was flat at $6,970 a tonne by 0720 GMT, from the previous session when it fell to a three-month low of $6,944 a tonne.               \par \par \uc2 * The most-traded May copper contract on the \uc2 Shanghai Futures Exchange\uc2  fell by 0.4 percent to 48,790 yuan ($7,900) a tonne, having descended to a new seven-month trough in overnight trade.               \par \par \uc2 * Russia paid a heavy financial price on Monday for its military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in neighbouring Ukraine, with stocks, bonds and the rouble plunging as President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's forces tightened their grip on the Russian-speaking Crimea region.               \par \par \uc2 * Manufacturing growth in Europe and Asia slowed last month, pressured by falling demand from abroad, while the United States bucked the trend with manufacturing expanding at its fastest pace in over three years.               \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  downplayed the yuan's recent fall on Monday, saying the world's second-largest economy is in a good shape and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline did not reflect fundamentals.               \par \par \uc2 * U.S. auto sales in February finished even with the year-earlier period as hefty incentives to lure customers into dealerships late in the month could not overcome cold and snowy weather.               \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Vale SA\uc2 's  Canadian unit has resumed work on its Copper Cliff Deep nickel project in the Sudbury basin and expects to complete a feasibility study by the end of the year, a company executive said on Monday.               \par \par \uc2 * For the top stories in metals and other news, click        , or                              \par \par \uc2 MARKETS NEWS               \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine drove up crude oil and prices for gold and government debt on Monday as the heightened tensions spurred investors to seek safe havens and sell any exposure to the region.               \par \par \uc2 DATA (GMT)               \par \par \uc2 1000 Euro zone Producer prices               \par \par \uc2 1445 U.S. ISM-New York index               \par \par \uc2 1500 U.S. IBD economic optimism                                             \par \par \uc2 PRICES               \par \par \uc2 Three month LME copper               \par \par \uc2 Most active ShFE copper               \par \par \uc2 Three month LME aluminium               \par \par \uc2 Most active ShFE aluminium               \par \par \uc2 Three month LME zinc               \par \par \uc2 Most active ShFE zinc               \par \par \uc2 Three month LME lead               \par \par \uc2 Most active ShFE lead               \par \par \uc2 Three month LME nickel               \par \par \uc2 Three month LME tin               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-4T02:43:55.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140304ea340025v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
