\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on March 4\b0\par\par\uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 05:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NAIROBI, March 4 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic\par indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves and political events may affect African markets on\par Tuesday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  *Uganda, Kenya central banks to announce the latest\par  decisions of their benchmark lending rates             \par              .\par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian shares were on the defensive on Tuesday as tensions\par  over Ukraine showed no sign of abating, with Russia\par  tightening its grip on Crimea while the West sought measures\par  to deter Moscow.                           \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Brent crude held above $111 on Tuesday, at its highest\par  levels since the end of last year, as tensions over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par  military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Ukraine rattled global markets and\par  stoked fears of energy supply disruption to\par  Europe.                    \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  SOUTH AFRICA MARKETS\par  South Africa's rand weakened alongside other emerging\par  markets on Monday as investors dumped high-yielding assets\par  in a wave of risk aversion fanned by political tensions in\par  Ukraine.                \par      Stocks fell for the first time in four sessions on\par  Monday as investors globally sold off risky assets on the\par  rising threat of war between Ukraine and\par  Russia.               \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigeria's naira firmed against the dollar on the interbank\par  market on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it will sell\par  dollars on forward delivery from Monday in its bid to shore\par  up the domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's value.                \par  \par  NIGERIA POWER PLANTS\par  Nigeria will accept offers from 42 prequalified bidders for\par  10 state-owned power plants on March 7, the privatisation\par  agency said on Monday, in a continuation of one of President\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goodluck Jonathan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's most important policies.               \par  \par  NIGERIA SECURITY\par  Islamist insurgents have killed at least 31 people in\par  attacks on a village in northeast Nigeria, a state lawmaker\par  said on Monday, a day after 85 were killed in a wave of\par  attacks by suspected militants nearby.                \par  \par  AFRICA TELECOMS TOWER FIRM\par  African phone tower group IHS has raised $420 million in\par  equity and $70 million in debt to fund its expansion across\par  the continent, the company said in a statement on\par  Monday.               \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  Kenyan shares were barely moved on Monday as investors\par  awaited more corporate earnings results from last year to\par  set the pace for the rest of the week.                \par  \par  KENYA REA VIPINGO\par  Kenyan sisal producer Rea Vipingo's          majority\par  shareholder, REA Trading, has raised its offer to buy the\par  rest of the company's shares by 75 percent.                \par  \par  KENYA TELECOMS\par  Kenya's two biggest telecoms operators, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Safaricom\f28 \uc2 \f2           \par  and the local unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel\f28 \uc2 \f2           , have made a\par  joint bid for the smallest operator, Indian group Essar\par  Communications' Yu, the industry regulator said on\par  Monday.                \par  \par  KENYA CMC HOLDINGS\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Al-Futtaim Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  is close to taking control of Kenyan car\par  retailer CMC Holdings          after 91 percent of\par  shareholders accepted its 7.6 billion shilling ($87.91\par  million) offer, the Dubai-based company said on\par  Monday.                     \par  \par  ECOBANK MANAGEMENT\par  Ecobank          shareholders passed a governance action\par  plan to address criticism by Nigeria's securities regulator\par  at an extraordinary general meeting on Monday where the fate\par  of CEO \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thierry Tanoh\f28 \uc2 \f2  was not on the agenda, a top bank\par  official said.                  \par  \par  IVORY COAST COCOA \par  Cocoa arrivals at ports in top grower Ivory Coast reached\par  around 1,101,000 tonnes by March 2 since the start of the\par  season on October 2, exporters estimated on Monday, up from\par  964,000 tonnes in the same period of the previous\par  season.               \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-7T04:50:31.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140304ea340073l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
