\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ.com What's News - Worldwide News Briefs For March 4\b0\par\par\uc2 992 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par G-20 INFLATION EASES AGAIN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rise in consumer prices slowed across the world's largest economies for a second month, driven by falling inflation rates in several developing economies. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOME THAI RICE FARMERS TO GET RELIEF \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Election Commission approved the government's request to disburse $616 million to pay farmers for rice bought months ago in a now-troubled subsidy program. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA TO REVIEW CORBY PAROLE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Convicted drug smuggler Schapelle Corby could be put back in prison in Indonesia if a TV interview by her sister is determined to have violated parole conditions. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AFGHANISTAN TO DISBAND CRUCIAL GUARD FORCE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Afghan government is moving to dissolve a crucial guard force that protects military supply convoys, international aid programs and foreign installations. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OBAMA PUSHES MIDEAST COMPROMISE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama met Israel's leader to press for movement on peace talks with the Palestinians, saying an agreement remains possible but will require bigger compromises from both sides. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BEIJING'S GDP GOAL UNDER NEW SCRUTINY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After years as a planning formality, China's official target for economic growth is posing a problem for the country's leaders amid confusion about the signals the goal sends--and whether it even matters. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SURVIVORS RECALL CARNAGE AND TERROR IN CHINA RAMPAGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Victims of a mass knife attack in southwest China recount a panicked stampede, hiding in darkness and the singular wail of hundreds of people screaming at once. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INFLATION THREATENS EURO-ZONE RECOVERY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A prolonged period of low inflation in the euro zone may derail the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bloc's fragile economic recovery, and must be fought with additional monetary stimulus,\f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief Christine Lagarde said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB CLOSELY MONITORING UKRAINE CRISIS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  must closely monitor the crisis in Ukraine even though the direct economic impact of the country on the euro zone is limited, ECB President Mario Draghi said, suggesting that policy makers are eyeing the potential for a broader shakeout from the conflict between Ukraine and Russia. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SYRIAN MISERY VISITS TURKISH STREETS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A growing number of Syrian refugees have resorted to begging on Turkish streets, a new measure of desperation for a generation fleeing civil war. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S.-ISRAEL TIES 'UNSHAKABLE,' NETANYAHU SAYS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Israel's Benjamin Netanyahu said the U.S.-Israel relationship remains "unshakable" as U.S. lawmakers reiterated their support for efforts to curb Iran's nuclear program. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PENTAGON SUSPENDS MILITARY TIES WITH RUSSIA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Pentagon is immediately suspending military relations with Russia as the latest of a quickening series of American moves to isolate Moscow over its military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Ukraine. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CAMERON: WORLD NEEDS TO SEND \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 RUSSIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  A MESSAGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world needs to send Russia a message that continuing down the path of violating Ukraine's sovereignty will have consequences, said British Prime Minister David Cameron. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHIP INSURER WARNS VESSELS IN UKRAINE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leading maritime insurer Skuld asked shipowners to keep crews aboard ship during calls to some Ukraine ports as Russian security forces tighten their grip in the region. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWITZERLAND ASSURES ON EU IMMIGRATION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Switzerland has assured the EU that the present agreement giving its citizens unrestricted access to the Swiss labor market will apply until 2017. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BIDEN URGES RUSSIA TO PULL BACK FORCES FROM UKRAINE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Vice President Joe Biden called Russian Prime Minister Dmitry Medvedev on Monday to urge Russia to pull back its forces from Ukraine and to support the 'immediate deployment' of international monitors. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.K. PROBLEM OUT OF MERKEL'S HANDS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By setting out the limits of what is possible, Angela Merkel injected much needed realism into the debate over Britain's relationship with the EU, writes Simon Nixon. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OSCAR LOSS MAY COOL PUSH FOR CLOSER LOOK AT INDONESIA KILLINGS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A groundbreaking documentary about the killing of hundreds of thousands of Indonesians in the 1960s has lost its bid for an Oscar, taking with it some of the nascent buzz around establishing a truth commission into a dark period in the Southeast Asian country. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITIGROUP AND MEXICO UNIT HIT BY SUBPOENAS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it and its Mexico unit had received subpoenas from the FDIC and U.S. attorney's office for Massachusetts, a disclosure that came days after the bank alleged it had found fraud in Mexico. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MASERATI UNVEILS NEW COUPE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian luxury sports car maker Maserati presented a coupe concept at the Geneva motor show as a likely addition to complete its product lineup. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par APPLE GOES ON HIRING BINGE IN ASIA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Apple is hiring hundreds of engineers and supply-chain managers in China and Taiwan as it attempts to speed product development and release a wider range of devices. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWEDEN: EU MUST SHARE REFUGEE BURDEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swedish immigration minister asks \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  to punish EU members that don't share the burden of accepting refugees in accordance with bloc's laws. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU MAY IMPOSE ARMS EMBARGO ON RUSSIA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  threatens action if Russia doesn't reverse its actions in Crimea and may also suspend talks on easing the visa process for Russians. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PLANS SPECIAL FORCE FOR ISLAND DEFENSE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan plans to create a 3,000-troop unit specializing in amphibious \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "as swiftly as possible." \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ OFFICIAL SAYS TAX WON'T CHOKE RECOVERY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The remarks by the BOJ's chief staff economist come in the face of growing expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be forced to further ease policy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ETIHAD ZEROES IN ON EUROPE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Abu Dhabi's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Etihad Airways\f28 \uc2 \f2  wants access to a pan-European network of Alitalia, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Air Berlin\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Air France-KLM\f28 \uc2 \f2  to fly more traffic East through Abu Dhabi, according to Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 James Hogan\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NORTH KOREA LAUNCHES TWO MISSILES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 North Korea on Monday launched two short-range missiles into the sea off the east coast of the Korean peninsula, South Korean authorities said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For continuously updated news from the Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 04, 2014 10:00 ET (15:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140304ea34002cp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
