\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  softer amid Ukraine tensions; steady yuan limits slide\b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2014\par 06:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah down on month-end corporate dollar demand\par     * Ringgit falls as some hedge funds sell\par     * Baht lower on gold importers, politics\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 27 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par eased on Thursday as the dollar gained on rising geopolitical\par tensions over the Ukraine, but losses were limited as the yuan\par steadied after recent losses.\par     The Indonesian rupiah fell as local companies\par bought the dollar for month-end payments. The Malaysian ringgit\par  eased on selling from hedge funds.\par     Thailand's baht slipped on dollar demand from some\par gold investors and sustained political unrest.\par     The dollar held near a two-week high against a basket of\par major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as Ukraine's protest leaders named ministers\par they want to form a new government following the overthrow of\par President Viktor Yanukovich.\par     Russia's President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vladimir Putin\f28 \uc2 \f2  ordered 150,000 troops to\par be ready for war games near Ukraine, prompting the United States\par to warn \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that it would be a "grave mistake" to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par militarily. \par     A wider conflagration in the Ukraine could spark a rush to\par safety and damage vulnerable emerging market assets. \par     The dollar also found support after data showed sales of new\par U.S. single-family homes surged to a 5-1/2-year high in January.\par  \par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, recovered some of their\par initial losses as spot yuan turned firmer.\par     "Ukraine may have indirect impact on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it\par will hurt sentiment on overall emerging markets. What is more\par important to Asia is the yuan," said Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     "It's hard to say the yuan is stabilising for now. The yuan\par will see more volatility even though its long-term appreciation\par trend remains intact," said Park, adding that regional units may\par fluctuate on the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Earlier, the yuan or renminbi briefly fell and remained\par below the official midpoint fixing, which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set\par lower, a trend that is likely to continue as Beijing prepares\par for market reforms. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit eased to the U.S. dollar on selling from\par leveraged funds and it fell versus the Singapore dollar\par .\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its earlier losses,\par tracking a rebound in its non-deliverable forwards.\par     Traders also expected oil importers to buy it for\par settlements.\par     "I am not sure if the dollar demand will persist. The game\par is to stay long a bit in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said a senior\par Malaysian bank trader, adding that the ringgit has room to\par strengthen to 3.2600 per dollar.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah eased on month-end dollar demand from local\par companies, while foreign and local banks bought the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par dips.\par     Traders looked for chances to add long positions on the\par Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , expecting further capital inflows.\par     "Sentiment is still bullish on the rupiah with funds still\par coming in," said a Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader.\par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht edged weaker on dollar demand from some gold\par investors for the precious metal, which fell almost 1 percent on\par Wednesday in New York, traders said.\par     The precious metal is popular among Thai investors, and\par slides in gold prices often prompt some to buy physical gold or\par futures. Investors might need the dollar to purchase the\par precious metal.\par     Investors were keeping an eye on Thailand's anti-corruption\par agency. It is to bring charges of negligence against Prime\par Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yingluck Shinawatra\f28 \uc2 \f2  later in the day as anti-government\par protesters demand her ouster. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.39         102.35       -0.04\par   Sing dlr        1.2661         1.2667       +0.05\par   Taiwan dlr      30.289         30.350       +0.20\par   Korean won     1066.20        1065.40       -0.08\par   Baht             32.58          32.53       -0.17\par   Peso             44.66          44.61       -0.11\par   Rupiah        11655.00       11635.00       -0.17\par  *Rupee            61.98          61.98       +0.00\par   Ringgit         3.2755         3.2700       -0.17\par   Yuan            6.1231         6.1248       +0.03\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight