\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Russia Moves Ruble Band Higher For 15th Time in 2014\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2014\par 07:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Lukas I. Alpert \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW--The Bank of Russia said Tuesday it has shifted the ruble's trading band higher for the fifteenth time so far in 2014, as continued selling pressure amid a broader emerging market slide has dropped the Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to its lowest point in five years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on its website that it moved the ruble's floating trading band 5 kopecks higher to RUB34.30-RUB41.30 against the euro-dollar basket, which is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main gauge of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The ruble was trading at 41.14 against the basket early Tuesday. Downward pressure on the ruble has intensified after the U.S. Federal Reserve said it would draw back from its bond-buying approach, signalling an exit from its easy-money policies.\par \par \uc2 At the upper end, the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells dollars and euros to ease downside pressure on the ruble -- as has been the case in the past few months. The bank buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ruble strengthens toward the lower boundary of the band. Once an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  allotment of $350 million is exhausted, it automatically shifts the corridor.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't planning to stop its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Elvira Nabiullina, said Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, will stick to its policy of reducing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and permit a more flexible ruble exchange rate starting in 2015, she said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lukas I. Alpert at lukas.alpert@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 04, 2014 01:29 ET (06:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140204ea24000ng\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
