\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-EMERGING MARKETS-Fresh turbulence drives down  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 , bonds again\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sujata Rao   \par \uc2 894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2014\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 31 (Reuters) - Fresh waves of turbulence engulfed emerging markets on Friday, with a renewed slide in the Russian rouble and a sharp rise in bond yields across the board despite policymakers' efforts to staunch the bleeding.\par \par \uc2 Signs grew that stress is increasingly spreading to central European countries such as Poland and Hungary, which fared relatively well in the first sell-off phase earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Poland delayed publication of its monthly debt supply plan until next week due to market turbulence and an overhaul of its pension scheme, a day after Hungary was forced to cut a T-bill action because of a 67 bps jump in yields.\par \par \uc2 "We are in a negative feedback loop of weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , higher interest rates, weak growth and capital outflows. This feedback loop needs to play out and that means at the end of the day EM assets need to become much cheaper," said \uc2 David Hauner\uc2 , head of EEMEA fixed income strategy and economics at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Only then will people come back to buy," he added.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the latest to wade in with assurances that it would act to soothe markets if needed, adding to earlier verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from India and \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as big rate rises in Turkey and South Africa.\par \par \uc2 But the Hungarian forint fell 1.5 percent to the euro , hitting two-year lows, while bond yields jumped 20 basis points across the curve.\par \par \uc2 "Fears are growing that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot stop the forint's fall in any other way, this will lead to an interest rate hike in the end," a bond trader in Budapest said.\par \par \uc2 In neighbouring Poland, 10-year bond yields rose 10 basis points to a 4-1/2 month high after the government delayed its debt supply plan and the zloty lost 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 The spotlight remains on the rouble. A rally that started late on Thursday proved short-lived, taking the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down more than 1 percent, back towards five-year lows against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plans for "unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " should the rouble stray outside a target band, had squeezed out short rouble positions on Thursday but the broad trend for flight was very much intact.\par \par \uc2 The lira and the rand fell almost 1 percent and South African domestic bond yields hit the highest since mid-2011, as markets priced in more rate rises in coming months.\par \par \uc2 In equity markets, MSCI's main emerging markets index traded just off 4-1/2 month lows and are on track for their biggest monthly loss since mid-2012.\par \par \uc2 Domestic emerging bond yields have risen around 40 basis points since the start of January and sovereign dollar bond yields have jumped about 50 bps this month on \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  indices.\par \par \uc2 Pressure is mounting on other emerging central banks to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with Mexico likely to warn later on Friday that it is ready to raise interest rates if needed. The peso is trading just off 18-month lows.\par \par \uc2 CHINA, FED, CENTRAL BANKS\par \par \uc2 BofA/ML's Hauner said the moves were being exacerbated by thinner liquidity, caused by the lunar New Year holidays across much of Asia including China where weaker-than-expected growth data was at least partly behind the latest sell-off of emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2 That added to jitters regarding the U.S. Federal Reserve, which confirmed on Wednesday it would shave another $10 billion from its monthly money printing.\par \par \uc2 "What's driving this is the fear of a Chinese slowdown and what I want to see is some kind of policy action from the People's bank of China (PBOC)," said \uc2 Lars Christensen\uc2 , chief emerging markets analyst at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  has slammed what he called a breakdown in global monetary coordination, saying developed countries could not "wash their hands" of the turmoil caused in emerging economies by their actions.\par \par \uc2 Christensen said that in the absence of PBOC input, emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or policy tightening, was unlikely to be effective.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indicated they will defend the rouble vigorously (but) my fear is a repeat of 2008 when they spent $200 billion to defend an artifical rouble peg," he said.\par \par \uc2 Russian 5- and 10-year bond yields rose to 16-month highs, pricing in the likelihood of an interest rate rise in February.\par \par \uc2 Russian weakness is partly behind the 2.5 percent tumble in the Ukrainian hryvnia, analysts said, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's biggest one-day loss since 2009.\par \par \uc2 But respite from the Fed or China is unlikely, analysts say, noting China wants to engineer a slowdown in its economy while the United States has flagged its plans well in advance.\par \par \uc2 Hauner expect more pain ahead for emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 "What's going on now is not the fault of the Fed," he said. "The turmoil is down to China but also the fact that EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rates were misaligned," he said. "We are now around fair value but as history shows us, any selloff in these has a tendency to overshoot."\par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par               \par For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par               \par For TURKISH market report, see\par \par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For RUSSIAN market report, see )\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-3T13:13:58.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140131ea1v00bn2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
