\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Weakens to New Low Versus euro\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh \par \uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2014\par 18:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble hit a new low against the euro Monday, but the selloff in emerging markets was not entirely to blame.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say the Bank of Russia's determination to let the ruble float freely from 2015 is also dragging the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve's plans to reel in stimulus and weak economic data from China have prompted investors to pull back from riskier bets in recent days. On Friday, what began as localized selloffs in emerging markets morphed into a broad flight to safety--a pattern that persisted Monday.\par \par \uc2 The Russian unit hit its weakest level ever of 47.72 rubles against the euro. It firmed 0.2% to 47.30 by the end of the day. Versus the dollar, the ruble eased 0.2% to 34.60 after briefly hitting 34.86, its weakest level since March 2009.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also shed 0.4% to 40.48 against the euro-dollar basket, a level last seen in early 2009.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently reduced its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the ruble. It now shifts the ruble's trading band five kopecks higher against the basket once the amount of accumulated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaches $350 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  discloses the boundaries daily.\par \par \uc2 Fewer \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would mean a faster but shorter depreciation of the ruble, said Maria Pomelnikova, an analyst at Raiffeisen Bank in Moscow. To defend the upper boundary of the ruble's trading band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells unlimited amount of dollars and euros.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Pomelnikova said she suspects the band was moved four times today and is now located at RUB33.70-RUB40.70. The band stood at 33.50-40.50 rubles early Monday.\par \par \uc2 Russia's sluggish economic performance is also weighing on the ruble. Bruised by diminished investment, the economy grew just 1.4% in 2013, the slowest pace since the crisis. Capital investment fell 0.3% on the year, official data showed Monday.\par \par \uc2 Russia was one of the worst performing emerging markets last year compared with precrisis dynamics, \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "Combined with overall global investor dissatisfaction with emerging market growth prospects, we take this news as cause for additional nervousness on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the bank said.\par \par \uc2 The trend could reverse this week as companies face tax payments at the end of the month that prompt exporters to convert foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into rubles.\par \par \uc2 "As soon as the ruble stops falling and shows stability for around a week, it is quite possible that there will be a rebound of more than one ruble," Ms. Pomelnikova said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 27, 2014 12:22 ET (17:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140127ea1r002jf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
