\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Scraps 'Targeted'  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Interventions \highlight\uc2 --Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh \par \uc2 491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2014\par 18:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would cut \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Russian ruble in a step toward floating the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 2015, a move that will likely accelerate its weakening.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will eliminate daily sales totaling $60 million Monday, preparing the market for when it ceases to support the exchange rate, the bank said. It will, however, continue larger sales of dollars and euros if the ruble rises toward the edge of a trading band.\par \par \uc2 The ruble slipped after the announcement, ending 0.7% lower at 38.7 against the euro-dollar basket.\par \par \uc2 "The ruble's volatility will increase and will be similar to that on other emerging markets. If funds leave emerging markets in the next few months, than the ruble is set to weaken," said Vladimir Kolychev, chief economist at VTB Capital in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 The ruble was off 0.8% at 33.3 against the U.S. dollar Monday. ING Bank forecasts it will weaken further to 35.7 rubles a dollar by the end of the year, as Russia continues to grapple with slow economic growth and high capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 The ruble weakened 8% against the basket last year amid concerns that investors would pull back from emerging markets as the U.S. Federal Reserve began to taper its bond-buying program.\par \par \uc2 Russia has long used its large foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the ruble against sharp depreciation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is shifting its monetary policy to focus on the stubbornly high level of inflation rather than the exchange rate by 2015, meaning it will manage liquidity in the economy through interest-rate policy only.\par \par \uc2 Government officials have said that a weaker ruble could help Russia's economy--buffeted by weaker prices and diminished demand for its commodities exports--which the government forecast would grow 1.4% last year. Growth slowed to 1.3% year-over-year in November, the most recent figures available,\par \par \uc2 A free-floating ruble could also help Russia to proceed with its ambitious plan to make the ruble a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and possibly a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the ruble within a floating range against a basket made up 55% of dollars and 45% of euros. It sells dollars and euros to ease downside pressure on the ruble when it hovers in the upper range of the band. In the lower range, it buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and in the middle it carries out no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That range is from 38.2 rubles to 39.2 rubles, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells $200 million a day to smooth out excessive volatility. When the total purchases or sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceed $350 million, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves the ruble band five kopecks either way.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 13, 2014 12:15 ET (17:15 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140113ea1d002kt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
