\par\par \b \uc2 *Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Lowers  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Size Needed To Move Ruble Corridor\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2013\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 10 Dec 2013 09:01 EDT *Accumulated \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trigger Lowered To $350 Mln From $400 Mln\par \par \uc2 10 Dec 2013 09:02 EDT *Bank Of Russia: Change To Decrease CB Influence On Market\par \par \uc2 10 Dec 2013 09:03 EDT *Bank Of Russia: Change To Boost Efficiency Of Interest Rate Policy\par \par \uc2 10 Dec 2013 10:08 EDT  Bank Of Russia Grants Ruble More Flexibility\par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its profile on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, giving investors more sway in determining the ruble's value as it moves to a new system of ensuring monetary stability that targets inflation rather than the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia keeps the ruble within a floating range against the euro-dollar basket, moving it by five kopecks if the amount of its accumulated purchases or sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeds a specific amount. Eventually though, the bank intends to scrap such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and let the ruble float freely, part of a new monetary policy focused on keeping inflation under control through the use of interest rates.\par \par \uc2 After widening the ruble's free-float zone in early October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday trimmed the amount of accumulated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to $350 million from $400 million. The ruble immediately slid to RUB38.30 per basket from levels of around RUB38.22, moving closer to the four-year low of RUB38.68 hit last week.\par \par \uc2 In the upper range of the band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells dollars and euros to ease downside pressure on the ruble, as it is the case now. It starts buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ruble firms toward the lower boundary and carries out no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the middle of the corridor.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved the corridor higher 26 times so far this year, and the ruble band now stands at RUB32.80-RUB39.80 versus the basket, comprised of $0.55 and 0.45 euros.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 10, 2013 10:08 ET (15:08 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131210e9ca001ox\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
