\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Bank Of Russia To Fully Switch To Inflation Targeting By 2015\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2013\par 14:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia To Switch To Floating Ruble By 2015\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  To Gradually Cut \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  In 2014\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia Sets Inflation Target At 4.5% For 2014, 2015\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia Sets Inflation Target At 4% For 2016\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia Sets Maximum Deviation Of Inflation From Target At 150 BPS Either Way\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia Sees Low Risks Of Importing Inflation In 2014\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia: External Demand Will Not Contribute To Domestic Economic Growth In '14\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia: Domestic Demand To Be Key Driver Of Economic Growth In '14\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:30 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Russia Sees 2013 Net Capital Outflow At $67B, $30B In 2014\par \par \uc2 13 Sep 2013 08:58 EDT DJ  Bank Of Russia to Target Inflation, Float Ruble by 2015\par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh and Olga Razumovskaya\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--\uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday it will fully switch to inflation targeting and float the ruble by 2015.\par \par \uc2 In its report on monetary policy for 2014-2016, which will be submitted to the government later this year, the Bank of Russia said it has set an inflation target of 4.5% for 2014 and 2015, and 4% for 2016, while setting the maximum deviation from the target at 150 basis points either way.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it would gradually reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2014, before floating the ruble by 2015.\par \par \uc2 The bank predicted in its report that domestic rather than external demand would be the key driver of the country's economic growth in 2014. It forecast 2013 net capital outflows at $67 billion, slowing down to $30 billion in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key rates unchanged and hinted there would be no changes to them in October. It also introduced a new key lending rate of 5.5% for providing and withdrawing liquidity.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Alexei Ulyukayev, the country's economy minister, said the utility tariff freeze would also keep annual inflation at 4.6% in 2014, compared with previous expectations of a 5% rise in consumer prices.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 13, 2013 08:58 ET (12:58 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130913e99d002pk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
