\par\par \b \uc2 Russia's c.bank shifts rouble's trading corridor\b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2013\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 12 (Reuters) - Russia has shifted the exchange-rate corridor for the rouble by five kopecks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday, following market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rouble's volatility against the dollar-euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket.\par \par \uc2 The new corridor extends from 32.25-39.25 roubles to the basket as of Sept. 11.\par \par \uc2 Under its managed float, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases its market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the rouble approaches the boundary of the corridor. Once an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  allotment of $400 million is exhausted it automatically shifts the corridor.\par \par \uc2 The approach is designed to smooth market volatility, not defend levels.\par \par \uc2 The rouble was trading on Thursday near five-week highs against the dollar-euro basket at 37.64 roubles by 0605 GMT. (Reporting by Lidia Kelly)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -C.BANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130912e99c0007v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
