\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Russia to Tolerate Quicker Ruble Weakening\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2013\par 11:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has curtailed the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to move the ruble's trading band, it said on its website late Monday, opening the door for a quicker weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started selling dollars and euros in order to tame the ruble's weakening in April and since then it has sold more than $13 billion and around 850 million euros ($1.12 billion), with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasing after the ruble fell to its 2013 low in August.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on its website that it made the move "in order to further increase flexibility of the exchange rate".\par \par \uc2 Keeping the ruble within a floating range against the euro-dollar basket, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will now move this corridor by five kopecks either way if the amount of its accumulated purchases or sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeds $400 million.\par \par \uc2 Previously, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to buy or sell $450 million to move the band, which it did 14 times this year, bringing the band to RUB32.20-RUB39.20 versus the basket on Sept. 4 from RUB31.65-RUB38.65 as of late 2012.\par \par \uc2 In the upper range of the band the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells dollars and euros to ease downside pressure on the ruble and starts buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ruble firms toward the lower boundary of the band. In the middle of the corridor the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carries out no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ING bank said in a research note that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision will result in "a bit quicker" five-kopeck shifts in the corridor should the ruble remain under selling pressure.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of the year, the ruble has weakened by nearly 9% against the dollar, hit by expectations of tapering of quantitative easing in the U.S., Russia's slowing economic growth and the economy ministry's comment that a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would benefit growth.\par \par \uc2 Denis Korshilov, head of fixed income, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commodities at Citi in Moscow, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision would be "neutral" for the market, but may also indicate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tolerates a further possible weakening in the ruble.\par \par \uc2 "The move fits the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-term strategy of cutting down its presense on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as it switches to inflation targeting. I don't think it will result in a deep weakening of the ruble," Mr. Korshilov said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said in the statement that the current seven-ruble width of the trading corridor was adequate for the needed scale of the ruble's flexibility.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com [ 10-09-13 0917GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130910e99a000cx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
