\par\par \b \uc2 Russia Finance Minister Says Sharp Ruble Volatility To Stop\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alexander Kolyandr   \par \uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2013\par 17:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ST. PETERSBURG--Sharp fluctuations in the Russian ruble will ease as the Bank of Russia moves to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stability, Russia's Finance Minister said Friday.\par \par \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2 , speaking on the sidelines of the summit of the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  industrial and developing nations, said the ruble's recent weakening has not been caused by "systemic reasons."\par \par \uc2 "The ruble is not weakening, it's fluctuating," he said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is focused on "maintaining the ruble's stability."\par \par \uc2 "There will be no sharp volatility of the ruble," he added.\par \par \uc2 The ruble has lost about 8.5% of its value against the U.S. dollar so far this year, as investors pull their assets from emerging markets. The Russian ruble has suffered much less than the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other developing nations, notably India and Brazil, as it is being supported by high oil prices.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth out daily volatility of the ruble, but by widening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading corridor and adjusting its boundaries in accordance with demand and supply it is moving it toward a freer-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Siluanov said the Bank of Russia "keeps everything under control," adding that the ruble needs no support from a newly created reserve fund of the five largest developing nations, collectively known as BRICS.\par \par \uc2 Write to Alexander Kolyandr at alexander.kolyandr@dowjones.com [ 09-06-13 1114ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130906e9960002z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
