\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Bank of Russia Head Sees Low Inflation As Main Task - Report\b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2013\par 16:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 3 Sep 2013 10:33 EDT *DJ  Bank of Russia Head: Quantitative Easing Not Solution To Slowdown- Report\par \par \uc2 3 Sep 2013 10:33 EDT *DJ  Bank of Russia Head Sees 2013 Inflation At 5% To 6% - Report\par \par \uc2 3 Sep 2013 10:33 EDT *DJ  Bank of Russia Head Sees More Volatile Ruble Exchange Rate - Report\par \par \uc2 3 Sep 2013 10:33 EDT *DJ  Bank of Russia Head: Slowing Growth Not Cyclical But Structural - Report\par \par \uc2 3 Sep 2013 10:33 EDT *DJ  Bank of Russia Head: Slowing Growth "Worrisome" - Report\par \par \uc2 3 Sep 2013 11:12 EDT DJ  Bank of Russia Head: Quantitative Easing Not Solution to Slowdown- Report\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Kolyandr\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of Russia won't introduce quantitative easing to battle the slowing Russian economy because such a policy would result in higher inflation, the bank's new chairwoman said in an interview Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina told state news agency Tass that quantitative easing, whereby a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pumps cheap money into a stagnating economy, would jeopardize the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's low inflation policy goal.\par \par \uc2 "[Quantitative easing] will ease the pain only for some time and will have no long-term impact on economic growth, as it will cause risks of higher inflation and higher capital outflow" she said.\par \par \uc2 Russia's economic growth stood at 1.2% in the second quarter, marking a sixth consecutive quarter of slowing expansion. It comes against a background of low investment, high capital outflow and declining demand for oil and other commodities, which is Russia's main source of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The government has cut growth forecast twice this year to 1.8% from an earlier projection of 3.6%, a far cry from about 5% target President Vladimir Putin set for a medium term.\par \par \uc2 "The slowing growth is not cyclical, but structural," she said, adding that only institutional changes and lower inflation can boost investment and growth.\par \par \uc2 Russia's inflation stood at 6.5% in July remaining above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 6%. which prevents it to cut lending rates.\par \par \uc2 Mrs. Nabiullina said she still expects inflation to be at between 5% and 6% in 2013, and confirmed a target range of between 3% to 6% in 2014. She said such a target would only be possible if the government agrees to rise regulated utility tariffs below inflation.\par \par \uc2 As inflation remains the Bank of Russia's main policy goal, the ruble's exchange rate may face more volatility in the future, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  admitted. \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abstains from sizeable \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as part of its inflation-targetting policy. Without the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's support the ruble lost about 8.5% of its value against the U.S. dollar since the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 Mrs. Nabiullina said she agrees with the government's estimate of capital outflow in 2013 at between $70 billion and $75 billion.\par \par \uc2 Write to Alexander Kolyandr at alexander.kolyandr@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 03, 2013 11:12 ET (15:12 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130903e993002zp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
