\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Kazakhstan pegs tenge to  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  basket, dilutes dollar focus\b0\par\par\uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2013\par 14:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Kazakhstan moves away from focus on dollar, to deter speculators\par \par \uc2 * New peg seen as a more predictable and flexible rate mechanism\par \par \uc2 By Mariya Gordeyeva\par \par \uc2 ALMATY, Aug 28 (Reuters) - \uc2 Kazakhstan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would peg the tenge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a similar system to that used by its close trade partner Russia.\par \par \uc2 The new system will start on Sept. 2, replacing a managed float of the tenge that used the dollar as a reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 National Bank Chairman Grigory Marchenko said the move aimed to move Central Asia's largest economy away from a pure dollar focus to an array of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that better reflects underlying trade flows, and to deter speculators.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar will account for 70 percent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the euro for 20 percent and the Russian rouble 10 percent, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 The initial rate of the tenge to the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be set at 113.7 tenge, Marchenko said.\par \par \uc2 "We do not rule out that hina's yuan can become part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in the future," he told a news briefing.\par \par \uc2 "The main advantage of introducing a multi-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket will be a gradual reduction of the role of the U.S. dollar on the internal market and in foreign trade."\par \par \uc2 Kazakhstan's economy relies heavily on exports to the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , China and large northern neighbour Russia. Kazakhstan's imports are dominated by Russia and China, which neighbours Kazakhstan in the southeast.\par \par \uc2 The vast Central Asian nation, which is a major producer and exporter of oil, industrial metals, uranium and grain, is a member of a customs union with Russia and Belarus.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  runs a managed float of the rouble against a target \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made up of dollars and euros.\par \par \uc2 The policy allows \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to use market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth volatility, without having to defend levels that might encourage a speculative attack.\par \par \uc2 "I think they are following in Russia's footsteps ... and the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket regime has worked quite well in recent years," said Tim Ash, analyst at Standard Bank.\par \par \uc2 "They (Kazakhstan) need to have a system which mirrors the rouble," said Barbara Nestor, emerging markets strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  London.\par \par \uc2 MOVING TO A MORE FLEXIBLE RATE\par \par \uc2 The steppe nation of 17 million, the second-largest post-Soviet oil producer after Russia, had previously used a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor which it dropped in 2011.\par \par \uc2 The new peg reflects Kazakhstan's "medium-term strategy of moving towards a flexible tenge", said one Moscow-based analyst who covers the former Soviet Union. "This is a first step on the road to a more flexible, floating corridor arrangement."\par \par \uc2 Marchenko said the peg to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket was set "to lessen speculative moods on the market".\par \par \uc2 "It will soften negative consequences of inflows and outlows of speculative capital ... which cause volatility of the tenge against the dollar," he said.\par \par \uc2 The official rate of the tenge rose to 152.16 per dollar on Wednesday from 152.47 in the previous trading session, and Marchenko said it would not be allowed to strengthen further below 152.\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold $1 billion in July and bought $800 million in August to help steady the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Short-lived weakening of the tenge to nearly 154 per dollar in recent weeks triggered an avalanche of speculation in Kazakhstan's social networks about its imminent depreciation.\par \par \uc2 "When the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was letting the tenge weaken, locals were worried that they might need to dollarise savings, because it was an unpredictable policy - this is a more predictable policy framework," said Nestor of \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  London.\par \par \uc2 KAZAKHSTAN-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 2) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | ABX | BNX | Z | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130828e98s000l5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
