\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Gains; US Retail Sales Eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 1,019 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2013\par 13:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Euro gains briefly on German ZEW indicator\par \par \uc2 --Dollar rises above Y98 against yen\par \par \uc2 --U.S. retail sales data, Chile rate decision on the agenda\par \par \uc2 By Clare Connaghan\par \par \uc2 The euro fell against the dollar Tuesday, despite signs emerging the long-running recession in the euro zone could be coming to an end.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose to the day's high of $1.3317 against the dollar, after a key indicator showed economic sentiment in Europe's largest economy--Germany--increased to its highest level since March. But the move quickly subsided and by 1056 GMT the euro was trading down at $1.3297.\par \par \uc2 "Generally there's a lack of activity and liquidity....there are still are lot of participants on the sidelines taking no active positions," said Aurelija Augulyte, a senior analyst at Nordea.\par \par \uc2 The Center for European Economic Research, or ZEW's, monthly indicator of expectations jumped to 42.0 in August, from 36.3 in July, beating expectations for an increase to 40.0 from economists surveyed by the Wall Street Journal ahead of the release. Economic expectations for the euro zone also jumped to their highest level since 2010.\par \par \uc2 "This is a good sign that the worst [of] the recession in the euro zone might be over," said Michael Schroeder, head of the international finance and financial management department at ZEW.\par \par \uc2 In a further positive sign, another data release showed industrial output in the 17 nations that use the euro rose at its fastest pace in more than two-and-a-half years during the three months to June.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the dollar rose above Y98 against the yen, as the Nikkei Stock Average jumped 2.6% to 13,867.00, the sharpest percentage gain for the benchmark since Aug. 2.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the pound had a choppy session against the dollar in the aftermath of data showing the annual rate of inflation fell to 2.8% in July from 2.9% in June. The focus now turns to Wednesday's unemployment release after the Bank of England said it will hold interest rates at record lows until the U.K.'s jobless rate falls 7%.\par \par \uc2 "Generally we expect that the pound will start to become a lot more sensitive to the labor market report, similar to what the dollar has started to do with payrolls ever since the Federal Reserve put their own explicit target in," said Chris Walker, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 In other news, the Norwegian krone rose to a three-week high against the euro after retail sales fell 0.2% in June, much less-than expected.\par \par \uc2 The krone's reaction to the data is fully justified, says Arne Lohmann Rasmussen, chief analyst at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 , "Together with the higher inflation last week it further removes the risk of a rate cut from \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead to later Tuesday, July's retail sales data in the U.S. due at 1230 GMT will in focus. Economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires see an increase in July of 0.3% from June.\par \par \uc2 In emerging markets, the Indian rupee strengthened against the U.S. dollar after the government raised import taxes on gold and silver, as part of its latest effort to curb an outflow of dollars and support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which fell to a record low last week. The dollar fell to as low as 60.90 rupees following the measures, down from around 61.10 before they were announced.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Bank of Russia raised the ruble's trading band for the second time this month to reduce the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking place amid a slide in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was moved five kopecks higher Tuesday to RUB31.95-RUB38.95 against its reference basket of euros and dollars. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the ruble within a floating range against the basket and moves it by five kopecks either way if the amount of its purchases or selling of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeds $450 million in a day.\par \par \uc2 Up ahead, \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to maintain the benchmark overnight lending rate at 5% later Tuesday, according to a poll of analysts.\par \par \uc2 At 1059 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.3298 against the dollar, up from $1.3300, late Monday in New York, according to trading system EBS.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at Y98.07 against the yen, compared with Y96.90, while the euro was at Y130.41, compared with Y128.86. The pound was trading at $1.5450 against the dollar, compared with $1.5463 late Monday in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 73.86 from 73.613.\par \par \uc2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1009 GMT     1.3306     97.91      1.5457     0.9277 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish    Bullish    Bearish    Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Bearish    Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.3084     94.08      1.5466     0.9382 \par 3rd Resistance    1.3367     98.59      1.5675     0.9390 \par 2nd Resistance    1.3345     98.18      1.5574     0.9335 \par 1st Re