\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Rouble hits 13-month low, \uc2 Uralkali\uc2  shares slump\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maya Dyakina   \par \uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2013\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, July 30 (Reuters) - Shares in Russia's top potash producer \uc2 Uralkali\uc2  plunged as much as 24 percent on Tuesday after it announced it is quitting the top potash cartel BPC, while the Russian rouble extended losses to hit multi-month lows.\par \par \uc2 At 1228 GMT, the rouble-denominated MICEX share index was 0.3 percent lower at 1,394 points, weighed down by the chemicals sector. The dollar-denominated RTS fell 0.6 percent to 1,334 points.\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Uralkali\uc2 , the world's largest potash miner by output, nosedived after the company said it would leave the Belarusian Potash Corporation (BPC) due to a "deadlock" over sales, a move it expects will cause global prices to plunge by 25 percent.\par \par \uc2 As the market leader it hopes it can boost sales volumes to offset a decline in prices but investors were not convinced.\par \par \uc2 "This may very well mark the end of supply discipline in the potash market and is negative for the entire potash space," a trader at a Western bank said.\par \par \uc2 Uralkali\uc2  shares were down 18.4 percent by 1400 GMT, after shedding 24 percent at one point. The news affected the rest of the sector.\par \par \uc2 The MICEX Chemicals index was down 10 percent. Shares in Acron , one of Europe's top 10 fertiliser producers, fell 9.8 percent, while stocks in Russia's Phosagro were down 11 percent on concerns about falling prices for the key fertiliser mineral.\par \par \uc2 Uralkali\uc2  also announced it was freezing its share buy-back programme launched in 2011.\par \par \uc2 "Shares of \uc2 Uralkali\uc2  will remain under pressure in the market in any attempt to recover, as without the support of the buyback programme the shares should trade at a substantial discount to global peers," said Kirill Yankovsky, a trader at Uralsib Capital.\par \par \uc2 The rouble weakened 0.3 percent to 37.79 against the euro-dollar basket, a 13-month low, as the tax payment period ended. It was also 0.3 percent weaker against the dollar at 32.92 and down 0.4 percent against the euro at 43.75.\par \par \uc2 The rouble is being weakened by local demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for dividend conversions and by expectations for a traditionally weaker current account surplus during summer months when imports of services rise.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is supported by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The level of 37.8 against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket is seen by traders as a major resistance level at which the bank increases selling of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to around $400 million per day from $200 million.\par \par \uc2 Demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's debut one-year refinancing auction on Monday, the first auction under a scheme to cut the cost of long-term funding for banks, fell short of market expectations. That has fuelled speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon cut policy rates to support the economy.\par \par \uc2 Interbank rouble overnight rates fell to 6.09 percent from 6.25 percent on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Some traders are now betting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could also widen the rouble's floating basket corridor to reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that drain rouble liquidity.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  last widened the corridor further to 7 roubles in July 2012.\par \par \uc2 "The widening of the corridor is the next logic step after such an auction," said Ivan Mikhailov, a dealer at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, Sergei Fishgoit, a dealer at Otkritie bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to widen the corridor while the rouble was in the zone of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Zlata Garasyuta and Vlasimir Abramov; Editing by Jason Bush and Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-MARKETS/ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130730e97u000i2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
