\par\par \b \uc2 Rouble erases gains vs basket, c.bank shifts floating band corridor\b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2013\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, June 26 (Reuters) - Russia's rouble erased earlier gains of up to one percent versus the dollar-euro basket on Wednesday before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it moved the floating trading band up, selling more than $2 billion to ease the rouble's fall in June.\par \par \uc2 Russia's treasury bond yields extended gains, while the rouble and stocks edged up, buoyed by easing concerns about the health of the world's biggest economies.\par \par \uc2 Reassurance that the United States may be strong enough to cope if the Federal Reserve scales back its stimulus programme and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China's pledge to prevent any lasting credit crunch soothed emerging markets after a sell-off.\par \par \uc2 At 1038 GMT the rouble was 0.4 percent weaker against the dollar at 32.95 and 0.4 percent stronger versus the euro at 42.90. The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was flat percent at 37.43 against the dollar-euro basket, propped up by local tax payments and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it shifted upwards the boundaries of the rouble trading corridor by five kopecks as of June 25.\par \par \uc2 Russia last widened the floating rouble corridor by 7 roubles in July 2012 - from 31.65 to 38.65 roubles - and decreased the amount of cumulative \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  necessary for the band to shift by 5 kopecks to $450 million.\par \par \uc2 "The market is only oriented to the weakening of the rouble and the tax payment period may only limit this," said Igor Akinshin, a trader at \uc2 Alfa-bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Artyom Biryukov, an analyst at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , had expected the boundaries to be shifted on Tuesday, taking into account cumulative \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around $50 million per day.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $2.2 billion since the start of June to June 24 to ease the rouble's fall, according to Reuters calculations.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has depreciated by just over 5 percent against the dollar since Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  first signalled on May 22 that the Fed may "taper" its bond buying programme, holding up better than the Brazilian real and Indian rupee, which have fallen by 8 and 9 percent\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages a flexible exchange-rate corridor to smooth volatility in the exchange rate, but does not seek to defend specific levels. Its oil-fuelled economy runs large surpluses on the current account, and while net capital outflows continue, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has an arsenal of half a trillion dollars in reserves at its disposal.\par \par \uc2 The rouble is seen undervalued by analysts at \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  Investment Research, as the long-term trend shows the rouble at 32.3 per dollar if oil prices are at $101 per barrel, suggesting some strengthening.\par \par \uc2 "On the other hand, we cannot exclude emerging markets investors adjusting their approach to evaluating risk, specifically moving to view the rouble as being in a 'devaluation' transition", \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "If the winds blow in this direction, the current rate could instead be seen as part of the 'new normal'".\par \par \uc2 The rouble is weighed by concerns about an economic slowdown that has led the government to support a weakening of the rouble to restore export competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 The yield on Russia's treasury bond, maturing in February 2027, fell 13 basis points to 8.09 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The market is close to bottom, and the majority of non-residents have already withdrawn their funds. Current levels will be attractive to Russian players when global markets stabilise," Ekaterina Leonova, senior analyst at \uc2 Alfa-bank\uc2 , said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-traded RTS stock index was up 1.3 percent at 1,260 points. The rouble-denominated MICEX was up 1.5 percent at 1,317 points, led by gains in \uc2 AFK Sistema\uc2 , up 4.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Uralsib raised its price target for Sistema's global depositary receipts to $34 from $33 per GDR, seeing an 82 percent upside potential after the oil-to-telecoms conglomerate announced it is selling a 49 percent stake in oil firm \uc2 Russneft\uc2  for $1.2 billion.\par \par \uc2 Preferred shares of \uc2 Bashneft\uc2  extended losses, falling 6.6 percent on concern prompted by a newspaper report that minority investors might lose out in any takeover by Rosneft.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Maya Dyakina)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-MARKETS/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130626e96q000j2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
