\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Russia Defends Ruble for First Time in 5 Months in April\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2013\par 17:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in five months to ease downward pressure on the ruble, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $663.1 million and 45.1 million euros ($59.1 million) from foreign exchanges reserves in April to smooth ruble volatility. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, after buying $714.9 million and EUR72.6 million in the first two months of 2013.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aiming to switch to a policy of inflation targeting over the next two years, is gradually paring its presence in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Higher flexibility of the ruble exchange rate makes the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  an absorber of external shocks, related to commodity market volatility, which are crucial for balance of payments in one of the world's largest oil and gas producers.\par \par \uc2 Keeping the ruble within a corridor of RUB31.65-RUB38.65 against a euro-dollar basket, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars and euros when the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades in the lower half of the range to avoid excessive ruble appreciation, while it sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ruble hovers in the upper half of the band.\par \par \uc2 The bank is inactive if the ruble trades between RUB34.65 and RUB35.65 versus the basket of $0.55 and EUR0.45.\par \par \uc2 In early April, the ruble weakened beyond RUB35.65 following a fall in oil prices amid rising global risk aversion, but returned to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -free zone April 25.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@dowjones.com [ 07-05-13 1525GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130507e957000u8\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Russia near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx